WEBVTT

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:04.130
At this rate, this planet...

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:10.890
It's an earthquake.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:11.980
Luna...

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:14.900
What?

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:18.500
What's that?

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.640
I think it's the inside of the volcano.

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.480
The magma's boilin' up!

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:46.510
I think it's stopped.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.280
Everyone, are you okay?

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.560
We're fine.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:51.760
Hey, look!

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.150
That's terrible!

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:57.500
Everythin's gettin' messed up.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.280
What's happening to this planet?

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:05.600
Abnormal tectonic activity is increasing.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:08.770
What do you mean, "Abnormal?"

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:13.590
At this rate, the ecosystem of this planet will collapse.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:14.820
Collapse?

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.320
Don't'cha have a regeneration program input into you?

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.540
I have several regeneration programs.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.560
But a larger disaster than was anticipated is occurring.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:30.200
This situation surpasses my abilities.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.680
Then what's going to happen next?

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:40.140
To combat changes as large as these, I must increase my power.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.830
What does that mean?

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:47.230
There is a power in you beyond what nanomachines can give.

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.190
I cannot yet analyze what this power is.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:56.300
But I have concluded that your power is necessary if I am to solve this problem.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.230
Do something yourself!

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.240
I have a duty to restore and protect the environment of this planet.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.480
You attacked us mercilessly, claiming people were unnecessary...

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.870
...and now you want to use us for your own purposes?

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:19.180
To combat changes like this, Luna, I need to discover how to use this new factor you possess.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.450
Mine?

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.250
Don't be so self-centered!

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:26.930
At this rate, I will be unable to find a solution.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:28.850
What do you mean?

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.740
Basically, he's given up.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:39.200
That's a machine for you! If you don't get the right program input by people, you can't do anything!

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.360
I'm not fond of that tone of voice!

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.960
That's right! 'N what'cha mean, "That's a machine for you?"

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.030
Survive was workin' his guts out to protect this planet.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:55.250
That has nothing to do with us, does it?

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.380
Howard...

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.250
Anyways, if this planet is in danger then we'd best escape from it as quickly as possible.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.100
We've finally made it this far, after all.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:07.030
But at this rate this planet...

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.100
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.840
If we don't escape soon we'll be wiped out!

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:18.800
But it's impossible to go now!

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:22.210
I'd have to confirm that there aren't any problems with the operation of the space ship.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.950
Then we should start checking it out right away.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:26.490
Let's go, Shingo.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.360
I'll come too.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:54.130
I cannot let any of you leave here.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.100
Stop it!

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:00.310
I need all of your power to protect this planet.

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:02.480
Then don't do this!

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.990
Anyways, you talk about protecting, but you don't know what to do.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.070
Exactly!

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:12.700
The first thing should be findin' out what's happenin' on this planet, and you can't do that.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.080
Exactly.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.160
Let us investigate!

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.350
We want to know what's happening to this planet too.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.130
So we'll investigate it.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.750
But in return, promise you won't attack us anymore!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.180
Yeah! That's the ticket!

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.100
Once we know the cause, we may be able to find a way to protect this planet!

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.530
I have analyzed all of the data and could not find an answer.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:44.640
There is no chance that you will find a new solution with further investigation.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:53.150
Now listen here! It was people who discovered the Law of Universal Gravitation, and iinstant ramen!

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.870
Instant ramen?

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.170
That's right!

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:02.600
People have the ability to realize connections between things that seem unrelated at first glance!

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.060
Yeah! That, that!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.880
People have a little thing called "Imagination."

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:11.490
Nothing will change if you keep us shut in here like this.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:12.460
Exactly.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.660
I think you ought to take a chance on the possibilities people's imaginations create.

00:07:42.130 --> 00:07:45.130
It seems pointless to keep you trapped here.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:49.630
But if I ever doubt your actions, I shall dispose of you.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:50.640
I understand.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:59.060
A'ight! I think we oughtta split into field investigation 'n data analysis groups!

00:07:59.530 --> 00:08:05.940
That's right. The field investigators will first head for the nearby main terraforming machine.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:08.750
There's also an inspection shaft that descends into the crater!

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.900
Data analysis will be me and Chako.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.450
Yeah, leave it to us!

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.750
Then let's go to the main terraforming machine.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.310
That's the main terraforming machine.

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:42.460
Tako said to wait here, but...

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.610
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:48.500
Please move aside!

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.360
My screw!

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:00.760
Everyone, look for it please!

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:02.330
It's my precious screw!

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.710
Power output cut off...

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:07.810
Will we be okay...

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.160
...with him?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.910
So this is the heart of this planet.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:14.380
Looks like it.

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:20.530
Even the data 'bout the nanomachines scattered around the planet's all here.

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.030
Let's get started.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.350
If there's somethin' you don't understand, I'll translate.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.580
Let's go.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.150
It's been a thousand years since I've been here.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:39.800
There's nothing but rocks.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.660
It's enough to give you the shivers.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.040
Was it like this a thousand years ago?

00:09:44.530 --> 00:09:48.160
Yes. A thousand years ago, this whole planet was like this.

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:49.920
But look there!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.310
It's pretty.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.480
Yeah.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:59.430
It's taken a thousand years to get this far.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.210
Though it's thoroughly become a place where people can live...

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:10.100
The ones who restored life to this planet were the people, including Adam's parents...

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.580
...and Survive.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:49.290
This is still in operation.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:55.810
From the volcanic gases produced here, infrared inhibitor particles are made and emitted.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:01.890
Terraforming machines like this are installed in all the volcanoes on this planet...

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:04.810
...to counteract the greenhouse effect on this planet.

00:11:05.300 --> 00:11:09.160
Thanks to that, the environment was restored such that animals could thrive again.

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:11.080
Yes, just like that!

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:16.630
Of course, Survive knows the greenhouse gas levels of the whole planet, yes?

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:18.990
Yes, of course.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:23.760
Which means we'll need to get data from the volcano itself.

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:27.770
Let's bring home rock and underground water samples!

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:35.560
Seismic and volcanic activity data, changes in day length, planetary-scale temperature changes...

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:42.760
No matter how I look at this data, the tectonic and climate changes just suddenly increased.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:44.110
It's true.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.290
The increases until now were greater than Survive's calculations.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:50.790
We hafta find the cause of that.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.010
It looks like they're there.

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.520
Come on in!

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.050
Where are we going?

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.320
Going down!

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:48.850
'Tako' used in the derogatory sense.
You moron!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.180
Stop it more gradually!

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.690
Ah, I beg your pardon.

00:12:57.610 --> 00:12:58.740
What's that?

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:00.500
A tunnel?

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.450
A hole dug for inspection purposes.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:08.340
We can take samples of lava which hardened at various times.

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.590
Can we take a sample from a thousand years ago?

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.350
Yes, we can!

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:16.060
For the sake of comparison, let's bring back samples from other periods as well.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:17.560
Of course.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.560
Please wait a moment!

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:38.790
Is it possible the cause is outside the planet?

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:40.180
What'cha mean?

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:46.400
I'm not exactly sure, but maybe it has something to do with the orbit of the planet itself.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.540
Like a Milankovitch cycle?

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:53.000
But that would only explain the climate change.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:56.000
But we have to think about this from every angle.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:59.670
If it was something obvious, Survive would have noticed it.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.800
That's right. Let's look into it.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.310
Yeah.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.290
The inspection shaft Tako mentioned.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.350
It's the magma!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.080
It's hot!

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:31.780
If this wall were not here, you would all melt in an instant.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:37.160
Because a refrigeration system is hard at work in here, you're safe!

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.670
Can we take some of this magma back?

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:41.670
Of course we can!

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:49.100
That won't melt?

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:53.300
It won't melt at the temperature of the lava, so don't worry.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:02.900
I've done perfectly.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.660
That startled me.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.480
Looks like the activity has increased again.

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:30.990
It really is scary.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:33.390
There's no use staying here long.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.200
Yes! Let's go back immediately!

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.400
Give us a break!

00:15:49.930 --> 00:15:51.840
I haven't done anything!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:53.080
Then...

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.890
Looks like a breakdown!

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.360
Did Survive do it?

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:02.150
No, it looks like a run-of-the-mill breakdown.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.500
Why would it break down?

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:07.440
Well it is a thousand year old machine.

00:16:07.510 --> 00:16:10.210
I expected something like this to happen eventually.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.310
Tell us that sooner!

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:13.890
Can't you do anything about it?

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:17.380
What was that sound?

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:21.270
What is it?

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.060
The refrigeration system has broken!

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:28.480
Chako!

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:29.150
Whazzup?

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.740
The elevator has stopped!

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:31.850
What'd'ya say?

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:34.060
Is it Survive's fault?

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:37.100
No, it's a real mechanical breakdown.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.620
Oh no! The refrigeration system is out of order too!

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.630
If we don't hurry, they'll die from the heat of the magma!

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:55.930
It's hot...

00:16:58.510 --> 00:17:00.200
Tako, calm down!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.030
Okay...

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.260
We can't control it from here!

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:22.740
At this rate, we'll all die.

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:38.000
Luna!

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:41.430
It's no use. I can't move it with my power alone.

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.750
Survive, save everyone!

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.780
Move the elevator!

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:49.140
Say something!

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:50.940
Survive!

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:56.380
There is not space in the tightly sealed elevator shaft for my drones.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.410
It is impossible to rescue them while they are down there.

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:05.530
Whaddaya think you're sayin'? At this rate, they'll all die of the heat!

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.630
You must be able to do somethin'!

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:08.860
Wait a moment...

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:11.920
Maybe we can use that airtightness to our advantage.

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:14.830
Survive, say somethin'!

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:16.930
Chako, never mind.

00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:17.750
But...

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.330
It's okay.

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.430
I have an idea!

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:28.210
Does it seem like you can do anything?

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.530
Please wait a moment.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.740
Everyone's at the limit of their strength!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.910
If only Chako or Shingo were here...

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:39.740
Hey, Tako! Get a grip!

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:41.740
Everyone!

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:44.080
Chako! Shingo!

00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:46.630
It's okay. We'll definitely save you!

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.060
Listen to what I'm about to tell you.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:53.600
The elevator has liquefied coolant gas in it for the refrigeration system.

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:57.170
But the refrigeration system is broken!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.800
We're just usin' the gas, so that doesn't matter.

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:01.400
What do we do?

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:02.710
Tear it out.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:06.730
What? If we do that, it'll get hotter even faster!

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:07.730
Just do it!

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.290
We should follow Shingo's orders.

00:19:10.590 --> 00:19:11.150
You're right.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:12.270
Tako...

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:14.340
Yes...

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:19.700
What are you doing?

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:25.180
Making the liquefied coolant gas expand explosively in the heat of the shaft.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.080
What?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:31.100
The shaft is airtight, so the pressure should push the elevator up quickly.

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:32.840
It's impossible! It's too dangerous!

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:35.710
It's people who decide what's impossible.

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:40.030
When you reach the top, use the arms to stay in place, and escape!

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:51.730
The possibilities of people's imaginations...

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:53.710
Okay!

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:56.680
Tako, just like I told you before.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:57.990
Okay, but...

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:00.010
You can do it!

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.490
Chako...

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:03.800
We're trustin' you with everyone.

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:04.810
Okay!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:06.950
Release it!

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:36.190
Please hang on tight!

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:47.000
Now, quickly!

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:50.490
Everyone, hurry!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:53.750
Hurry!

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:54.880
Just a little longer...

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:03.760
--Kaoru!
--Tako!

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:14.450
We did it!

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:17.260
Thanks, Survive!

00:21:30.610 --> 00:21:33.050
Survive saved us.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.250
This is...

00:21:49.810 --> 00:21:51.130
Have you figured something out?

00:21:51.840 --> 00:21:55.290
The crystalline composition of the sample from a thousand years ago is different.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:56.020
As I thought.

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:58.520
What do you think that means?

00:21:59.300 --> 00:22:02.980
A thousand years ago, a large change in gravity may have occurred.

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:05.230
Such a thing is impossible.

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:11.340
Nothing could cause such a change in gravity short of a giant meteorite.

00:22:12.280 --> 00:22:15.840
Nothing like that has occurred these thousand years.

00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:19.790
What about the possibility that the effect came from outside the planet?

00:22:20.260 --> 00:22:21.310
What do you mean?

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:24.430
We came up with a hypothesis.

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:29.080
If somethin' like that caused the problems a thousand years ago,

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:32.040
the same thing might explain the current situation too.

00:22:32.040 --> 00:22:33.430
What's that?

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:36.560
The gravity storm.

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:38.710
The gravity storm?

00:22:46.030 --> 00:22:46.950
What's that?

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:07.360
Accordin' to Survive, the gravity storm'll smash into this planet in three days.

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:10.660
We have no choice! We have to escape in the space ship right away!

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:13.100
But we can't just abandon this planet!

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:17.040
We need this space ship to destroy the gravity storm!

00:23:17.230 --> 00:23:20.900
Why do we have to be sacrificed for this planet?

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:24.010
I'm definitely going back to the colony in this space ship!

00:23:25.510 --> 00:23:28.400
Next time: Because everybody likes this planet.
